The clock's description tells the counts a millisecond where it should tell the default span,
the largest power of two of counts within it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a description differs from the capability it describes
Witness: fuzz describe-every-type

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -1108,7 +1108,7 @@ static __attribute__((noinline)) int cap_info(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t *a
     case CAP_CLOCK:
         /* The rate and the default span, not the time, so no RIGHT_R. */
         arg[2] = timer_counter_hz();
-        arg[3] = timer_default_span();
+        arg[3] = timer_step_counts();
         break;
     case CAP_THREAD: {
         /* How many places it has, and the cores whose time they hold, a bit each. */
